{
	"_comment": [
		"Default armor plans, HAND-AUTHORED PER HULL. Keyed by hull id.",
		"PRE-FILL ONLY: blueprint_manager._deserialize_armor() expands the entry",
		"into per-facet assignments when a blueprint carries no 'armor' block at",
		"all - i.e. a fresh hull selection in the Design Lab. Every saved v3",
		"blueprint writes an explicit 'armor' block, so loading a save never",
		"consults this file and changing it can never alter an existing design.",
		"A hull with no entry here simply loads bare, exactly as before.",
		"Sides are the six ArmorPaint.SIDES brush sets; materials are",
		"ArmorPaint.PAINT_TYPE_IDS; thickness is 0.5-3.0. An omitted side is",
		"deliberately unarmored. Overlapping brush sets resolve in",
		"ArmorPaint.SIDE_PAINT_PRIORITY order, front last so a glacis wins.",
		"Static-defense (is_foundation) hulls DO get plans: they weigh 0.0 and",
		"have no drivetrain, so armor weight cannot overload them.",
		"This is NOT a hull sidecar - assets/models/hulls/*.json are regenerated",
		"wholesale by tools/blender/build_vehicle_hulls.py and would lose it."
	],
